    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 100.0%; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Primary appendiceal tumour</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Histological criteria in the primary tumour</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Terminology for potential peritoneal metastasis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Grading criteria for peritoneal metastases<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Low-grade appendiceal mucinous neoplasm</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Circumferential proliferation of mucinous epithelium with low-grade cytological features and pushing, diverticulum-like extension into or through the wall</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Low-grade mucinous carcinoma peritonei</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Hypocellular mucinous deposits</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Strips of neoplastic epithelium with low-grade cytological features</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">No infiltrative-type invasion by small glands, mucin pools, or signet-ring cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">High-grade appendiceal mucinous neoplasm</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Circumferential proliferation of mucinous epithelium with high-grade cytological features and pushing, diverticulum-like extension into or through the wall</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">High-grade mucinous carcinoma peritonei</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Hypercellular mucinous deposits as judged at 20&times; magnification</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Strips and clusters of neoplastic epithelium with high-grade cytological features (at least 10% of tumour epithelium)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Foci of infiltrative-type invasion by angulated glands in a desmoplastic stroma, or numerous small mucin pools containing clusters of tumour cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">High-grade mucinous carcinoma peritonei with signet-ring cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Infiltrative signet-ring cells with desmoplasia or single cells floating in mucin pools<sup>b</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"25%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Generally, the grade of the tumour in the appendix is concordant with that of the peritoneum. The grade of the peritoneal tumour has a greater effect on prognosis than that of the appendiceal primary tumour in discordant cases.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>b</sup>At least 10% of the tumour should be signet-ring cells for this designation. Signet-ring cells in mucin must be distinguished from degenerate tumour cells in the mucin (pseudo&ndash;signet-ring cells).</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
